(7758943, 1284430, 138630, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by kasaba:</b></div><hr/><i> Congrats and well done on the "colour change". Which method did you use? I find my colours often go "muddy" when I change them, so I am keen to learn :-). </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>I''ll update description to address that, Gaby <img border="0" src="https://www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif" xalt="'' . substr(''https://www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif'', strrpos(''https://www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''"/> <a href="https://www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=141319" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">kasaba</a><br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2023-10-16 13:06:13.</i></td>', 'Originally posted by kasaba: Congrats and well done on the "colour change". Which method did you use? I find my colours often go "muddy" when I change them, so I am keen to learn :-).   I''ll update description to address that, Gaby  kasaba', '2023-10-16 13:45:55.000000', '2023-10-16 14:06:13.000000', 0),
(7758969, 1284460, 55542, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by mariuca:</b></div><hr/><i> Independently of how I feel about the landscape (I gave 5 only because I have my own problems with  pictures  of landscapes that can be too close to a postcard) I salute Roberts close examination.  Reminds me what we used to do at DPC and how much we learned here </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>I totally agree and was thrilled to receive the comments and really appreciated the time Robert took to evaluate and make the suggestions that he did.</td>', 'Originally posted by mariuca: Independently of how I feel about the landscape (I gave 5 only because I have my own problems with  pictures  of landscapes that can be too close to a postcard) I salute Roberts close examination.  Reminds me what we used to do at DPC and how much we learned here   I totally agree and was thrilled to receive the comments and really appreciated the time Robert took to evaluate and make the suggestions that he did.', '2023-10-17 10:45:12.000000', NULL, 0),
(7758974, 1284456, 117474, '<td valign="top">I didn''t notice gold vs. orange in this one. <br/> <br/>However, when I saw this it immediately reminded me of a scene from the book "Jonathan Strange and Mr. Norrell" by Suzanna Clarke where Norrell compels all of the figures in a church to be magic''ed into animation, and they all spend the morning wandering around the church and telling anybody who''ll listen of what has happened over the last few centuries to anybody watching. This could be the church that I had in my minds eye (though perhaps a little more gothic).</td>', 'I didn''t notice gold vs. orange in this one.  However, when I saw this it immediately reminded me of a scene from the book "Jonathan Strange and Mr. Norrell" by Suzanna Clarke where Norrell compels all of the figures in a church to be magic''ed into animation, and they all spend the morning wandering around the church and telling anybody who''ll listen of what has happened over the last few centuries to anybody watching. This could be the church that I had in my minds eye (though perhaps a little more gothic).', '2023-10-17 14:35:22.000000', NULL, 0),
(7758978, 1284456, 30214, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by NiallOTuama:</b></div><hr/><i> This could be the church that I had in my minds eye (though perhaps a little more gothic). </i></td></tr></table> Yeah, this is a Norman chapel, quite different from the later Gothic style.</td>', 'Originally posted by NiallOTuama: This could be the church that I had in my minds eye (though perhaps a little more gothic).  Yeah, this is a Norman chapel, quite different from the later Gothic style.', '2023-10-17 18:22:23.000000', NULL, 0),
(7759115, 1284194, 193969, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by wolf:</b></div><hr/><i> Be interested to know how you took this.  My bucket list includes capturing the milky way. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>With a specialized Astro camera on an equatorial tracking mount.  You have to get 4 hours outside of Los Angeles to capture the Milky Way, and a tracking mount is not really necessary.</td>', 'Originally posted by wolf: Be interested to know how you took this.  My bucket list includes capturing the milky way.   With a specialized Astro camera on an equatorial tracking mount.  You have to get 4 hours outside of Los Angeles to capture the Milky Way, and a tracking mount is not really necessary.', '2023-10-20 22:02:17.000000', NULL, 0);
